---
const parts = [
  {
    name: "Where am I",
    primitive: "<Message>",
    text: "The first line names the thing and its parent, like a title bar.",
  },
  {
    name: "What is here",
    primitive: "<Message> + <Display>",
    text: "A short summary of what matters. Display carries the rows.",
  },
  {
    name: "Where next",
    primitive: "<Action>",
    text: "Two to five buttons with the ids filled in. The agent taps; it never guesses an id or a tool.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section">
  <p class="section-number">01</p>
  <h2>Every reply is a screen.</h2>
  <p class="section-text">
    A person moves through an app screen by screen. Good AX gives an agent the same thing:
    each tool result says where it is, what is here and what it can do next.
  </p>
  <div class="grid">
    {
      parts.map((part) => (
        <article class="card">
          <h3>{part.name}</h3>
          <p>{part.text}</p>
          <code>{part.primitive}</code>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p class="section-more">
    <a href="/guides/introduction/#think-in-screens">Read Think in screens →</a> the rules, and what each primitive
    sends to the model.
  </p>
</section>
